<section class="sec" id="trust" aria-labelledby="trust-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <div class="titles"><p class="eyebrow">Control and trust</p><h2 id="trust-h">Your network, your keys, your records.</h2></div>
      <p class="lead">Merit Order is software you run, not a service you send prompts to.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cols four">
      <div class="col"><h3>Self-hosted</h3><p>Docker Compose or a Helm chart. Your keys, your network, your Postgres and Redis. Signed multi-arch images when a version is tagged.</p></div>
      <div class="col"><h3>AGPL-3.0, every line</h3><p>Read, change and run all of it. If you change it and offer it to others over a network, you share your changes under the same license.</p></div>
      <div class="col"><h3>No content stored by default</h3><p>The ledger and session table hold metadata: hashes, timestamps, token counts, costs. The response cache, stored Responses and batch files are opt-in or explicit, and sealed.</p></div>
      <div class="col"><h3>Every decision recorded</h3><p>Each request keeps its routing reason, for example <code>coding: 32 tools; simple task wording (write (unit )?tests): level 2</code>, and the chances and costs it compared.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

